2	 * Connector-contributed agent tooling — deployment-time resolution.
3	 *
4	 * A connection whose connector declares `agentTooling` contributes three things
5	 * to the agent's sandbox: nix packages (so the CLI is on PATH), env vars (so it
6	 * is authenticated), and egress domains (so it can reach the provider). This
7	 * module turns the org's connection rows into that contribution; the deployment
8	 * manager applies it to the worker environment.
9	 *
10	 * The declaration is read from `connector_definitions.agent_tooling` — the
11	 * database, never connector code. Nothing here loads or executes a connector.
12	 */
